  <media:group>
   <media:title>Omotenashi In Action</media:title>
   <media:content url="https://www.youtube.com/v/LgQibCpm3cQ?version=3" type="application/x-shockwave-flash" width="640" height="390"/>
   <media:thumbnail url="https://i1.ytimg.com/vi/LgQibCpm3cQ/hqdefault.jpg" width="480" height="360"/>
   <media:description>At Mazda, people are at the heart of everything we do. From the way we design our vehicles to the way we support our employees, dealers, and customers, our philosophy begins with a simple belief: meaningful experiences are created by putting people first.

More than hospitality, Omotenashi is a philosophy centered on anticipating needs, building meaningful relationships, and creating exceptional experiences for others.

In this employee story, Kathy Barth shares how Omotenashi shapes the way she approaches her work, supports Mazda's dealer network, and builds lasting relationships every day. Through her experiences, you'll see how this mindset comes to life across Mazda North American Operations and how it helps foster a culture centered on empathy, collaboration, and service.

